{"availability":"available","full":"JakeChampion/lang","name":"lang","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Go","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-06T07:50:20Z","updated":"2026-10-04T08:08:41Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://jakechampion.github.io/lang/playground/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:01.320Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:01.320Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:01.320Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:13:46.323Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-04T08:16:01.320Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Fern is a small, statically typed, general-purpose language that compiles to a static native binary or to WebAssembly from the same source. It has no runtime to boot and no garbage collector: memory is reference counted, with the counting largely elided at compile time. A hello-world binary is a few kilobytes and startup is the kernel's exec followed by your main.","The compiler is a single binary. It parses, type-checks, optimises, assembles, and links in-process, so building a program needs nothing on PATH but fern itself. The same binary formats, lints, type-checks, interprets, resolves packages, and reports what capabilities a package reaches.","Documentation: (tutorial · reference · standard library · playground · why Fern)"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JakeChampion/lang/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e13a898bdfadca1372a06096d91830048d12436b349292e230d29b0e623c37be","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T22:13:46.420Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:37.264Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Fern is a small, statically typed, general-purpose language that compiles to a static native binary or to WebAssembly from the same source. It has no runtime to boot and no garbage collector: memory is reference counted, with the counting largely elided at compile time. A hello-world binary is a few kilobytes and startup is the kernel's exec followed by your main.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JakeChampion/lang/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"The Fern one under examples/selfhost/ is where the language now lands: it compiles itself to a byte-identical fixpoint (make distcheck) and builds every program in coreutils/. make bootstrap builds it from a checkout with no Go installed, using a pinned earlier release (docs/BOOTSTRAP.md), and make selfhost-cli builds it with the Go compiler for the host you are on.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JakeChampion/lang/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"required","text":"It is the stage-0 bootstrap and the differential oracle, and accepts only bugfixes, oracle needs, and what the self-host sources need to build (docs/NATIVE-FREEZE.md, docs/NATIVE-CONVERGENCE.md).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JakeChampion/lang/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"e13a898bdfadca1372a06096d91830048d12436b349292e230d29b0e623c37be","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JakeChampion/lang/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:37.264Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T08:08:41Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JakeChampion/lang/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:37.264Z","hash":"e13a898bdfadca1372a06096d91830048d12436b349292e230d29b0e623c37be","originalBytes":9535,"storedBytes":9535,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["fern","docs","examples","binary","internal","compiler","make","build","hello.fern","static","every","target","cmd","coreutils","i32","native","run","same","backend","compile","elf","gnu","host","in-process","language","let","print","reference","return","std","string","test","under","what","apple","arm64","bootstrap","builds","capabilities","code","compiles","component","hello","linux","one","only","place","program","rect","r